course: dictionary
lesson: 8883
title: One word, many meanings: show
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Show is a small word with many jobs. You can find out which meaning it has by reading the words around it. «The graph shows the results.» A graph cannot watch anything, so show means make clear: the graph makes the results easy to see.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. «Show me how to tie a knot» needs show to mean explain how to do something. In «We went to a show on Saturday», show is a noun, a thing to watch like a play or a concert.
explain: Show can be a verb or a noun, and it changes its form: show, shows, showed, shown, showing. «In 1609-1610 Galileo's homemade telescope showed moons going round Jupiter» uses showed, the past tense. It let people see the moons.
fact: Show (verb) means to let someone see something.
fact: Show (verb) can also mean to explain how to do something, or to make something clear.
fact: Show (noun) means something to watch, like a play, a concert or a TV programme.
fact: «Showed» is the past of show. «Shown» is often used with has or have, as in «has shown».
fact: «Show off» means to boast, to try to make people admire you, as in «The Zebra and the Giraffe show off their trick».
exercise: «The Zebra and the Giraffe show off their trick.» What does show off mean here? | To close the curtains | To hide behind a tree | To explain the rules slowly | *To boast and try to be admired
exercise: «In 1609-1610 Galileo's homemade telescope showed moons going round Jupiter.» What does showed mean here? | Shouted about | Painted | *Let people see | Hid from
exercise: Find and copy the word that means makes clear in «Some pictures, like the duck-rabbit, can be seen in two ways, which shows that seeing is partly guessing.» | pictures | *shows | duck-rabbit | partly
test: «We watched a show on TV last night.» Which meaning of show fits? | Explain how to do something | Let someone see something | *Something to watch, like a programme | Make something clear
test: Which word is the past tense of show? | showy | *showed | showing | shows
exam: «Please show me how to fold the paper.» Which meaning fits? | *Explain how to do something | A flower show with prizes | A TV programme you watch | To boast and try to be admired
